+## 5. Phase 3 (KAN-428) Credential & Container Checklist
+
+The following prerequisites, environment configurations, and test fixtures are required to execute the live Phase 3 workouts (`KAN-428`):
+
+### 5.1 Container & Runtime Environments
+1. **Primary Multi-Container Testbed:**
+   - PostgreSQL 16+ instance running with `FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY`.
+   - Redis or PostgreSQL notification listener for real-time WebSocket event bus.
+   - `kanban` application container running with `APP_ENV=test` and `KANBAN_SECRET_KEY` configured.
+2. **Standalone Single-Container Testbed:**
+   - Standalone `docker run` deployment testing behavior when nsjail is not available.
+   - Verified fallback: Tier A WebAssembly execution functional; Tier B nsjail gracefully disabled in UI.
+
+### 5.2 Test Principals & Credentials
+1. **Primary Workspace Admin:**
+   - Handle: `@admin` (or primary test workspace admin)
+   - Credentials: Known test password + enrolled WebAuthn passkey / TOTP secret for AAL2 step-up verification.
+2. **Secondary Independent Workspace Admin (Mandatory for Dual-Control Escalation):**
+   - Handle: `@security-admin` (distinct from script author)
+   - Credentials: Test password + enrolled TOTP secret for AAL2 signing of escalation requests.
+3. **Standard Project Member:**
+   - Handle: `@developer` (role: `MEMBER`)
+   - Credentials: Standard credentials to verify access restrictions on admin-only settings.
+
+### 5.3 Test Fixtures & External Assets
+1. **Pre-Compiled Test WebAssembly Module:**
+   - Minimal Wasm binary (validating issue summary length or setting default priority) uploaded to `POST /api/v1/projects/{key}/wasm-modules` to generate a known manifest SHA256 digest.
+2. **Sample Git Repository:**
+   - A public read-only bare mirror repository (e.g. `https://github.com/ThumbsUp-HQ/kanban.git` or local test bare repo) with branch `main` to validate git binding and refresh workflows.
+3. **AI Provider Fixture:**
+   - Local Ollama instance (`http://localhost:11434`) or Gemini test API key configured to test Agent-based workflow transition hooks without incurring third-party network costs.
